{
  "title": "CASE and conditional aggregation",
  "summary": "Turn values into categories, then count each category in one pass.",
  "minutes": 12,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "CASE: if/else inside a query",
      "body": [
        "`CASE` picks a value by testing conditions in order:",
        "",
        "```sql",
        "SELECT id, minutes,",
        "       CASE",
        "         WHEN minutes < 10 THEN 'short'",
        "         WHEN minutes < 30 THEN 'medium'",
        "         ELSE 'long'",
        "       END AS length_band",
        "FROM rides;",
        "```",
        "",
        "- The **first** true `WHEN` wins, so order matters.",
        "- With no `ELSE`, an unmatched row gives NULL.",
        "- There's a short form for equality: `CASE plan WHEN 'member' THEN 'M' ELSE 'C' END`."
      ]
    },
